{"chunk_id": "892f4b81c4bc", "text": "As Vibhishana, brother of Ravana, seeks refuge with Rama, the monkey leaders debate whether he should be trusted. Some argue that abandoning one\u2019s own brother in crisis proves treachery and that the demon may be a spy sent by Ravana. Rama listens carefully but explains that political realities often divide royal families and that motives\u2014such as ambition or disgust with Ravana\u2019s cruelty\u2014could explain Vibhishana\u2019s defection. More importantly, Rama declares a moral principle greater than strategy: anyone who approaches him seeking refuge must be protected, even if he were an enemy. Citing sacred teachings and the story of a pigeon who sacrificed itself to shelter a foe, Rama affirms the dharma of sanctuary, revealing both his confidence in his power and the ethical foundation of his kingship.\nRama hears the monkeys\u2019 doubts about Vibhishana but declares that anyone seeking refuge\u2014even an enemy\u2014must be granted protection.\nThemes: refuge and protection, kingship ethics, trust versus suspicion, dharma and compassion", "vector": [0.0020467175636440516, -0.04028628021478653, -0.001310196821577847, -0.017286332324147224, -0.007313956972211599, 0.015553731471300125, -0.005108527839183807, -0.01735246181488037, -0.02999648079276085, -0.007598315365612507, 0.011202389374375343, -0.00753879826515913, 0.016069544479250908, 0.00012781652912963182, -0.02231219783425331, -0.0004947336274199188, 0.047269586473703384, -0.03592171147465706, 0.031001655384898186, -0.013444189913570881, -0.008808490820229053, -0.0036933498922735453, -0.021478962153196335, -0.006232734769582748, -0.01249853428453207, 0.020553145557641983, 0.028700336813926697, -0.024137381464242935, 0.008801877498626709, -0.010402219370007515, 0.004486907739192247, -0.00691717816516757, 0.009006880223751068, 0.0008671271498315036, -0.019547970965504646, -0.004166177939623594, 0.007717348635196686, -0.0005344115197658539, 0.03393781930208206, -